<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Alexander of Greece</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1893–1920</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Alexander was king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/greece">Greece</a> from 1917 to 1920. He was put on the throne in place of his father <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/constantine-i">Constantine I</a>, whom the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/allies">Allies</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eleftherios-venizelos">Eleftherios Venizelos</a> forced into exile for his neutral stance in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-world-war">First World War</a>, and he had little political power. He died in October 1920 of an infection after a bite from a pet monkey, which led to the return of Constantine I.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/alexander-of-greece.jpg" alt="Alexander of Greece" width="320" height="446" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Charles Chusseau-Flaviens · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:King_Alexander_of_Greece.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
